{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc '/tools/ladon --help'","aggregated_output":"usage: -c [-h] [--repo-root REPO_ROOT] [--root ANALYSIS_ROOTS]\n          [--scope {changed-set,closure,inventory,multi-root,namespace,owner}]\n          [--changed-path CHANGED_PATH] [--changed-manifest CHANGED_MANIFEST]\n          [--max-modules MAX_MODULES]\n          [--max-context-modules MAX_CONTEXT_MODULES] [--cache-dir CACHE_DIR]\n          [--no-cache] [--build] [--build-timeout BUILD_TIMEOUT]\n          [--extraction-backend {text,lean}]\n          [--lean-extraction-scope {root,inventory}]\n          [--lean-cache-dir LEAN_CACHE_DIR]\n          [--lean-batch-size LEAN_BATCH_SIZE] [--lean-timeout LEAN_TIMEOUT]\n          [--lean-strict] [--progress {auto,plain,json,off}]\n          [--overall-timeout OVERALL_TIMEOUT] [--max-rss-mib MAX_RSS_MIB]\n          [--max-report-bytes MAX_REPORT_BYTES] [--format {text,json}]\n          [--output OUTPUT] [--emit FORMAT=PATH] [--report-version {v3,v2,v1}]\n          [--projection {summary,review,full}] [--output-json LEGACY_JSON]\n          [--output-text LEGACY_TEXT] [--fail-on FAIL_ON]\n          [--generated-at-utc GENERATED_AT_UTC] [--doc-file DOC_FILE]\n          [--packet-dir PACKET_DIR]\n          [--architecture-policy ARCHITECTURE_POLICY]\n          [--source-pattern-policy SOURCE_PATTERN_POLICY]\n          [--generated-family-policy GENERATED_FAMILY_POLICY]\n          [--generated-family-candidate-profile GENERATED_FAMILY_CANDIDATE_PROFILE]\n          [--module-system-witness MODULE_SYSTEM_WITNESS]\n          [--import-diet-witness IMPORT_DIET_WITNESS]\n          [--proof-xray PROOF_XRAY]\n          [--packet-profile {generic,review_packet,witness_bundle,release_bundle}]\n          [--verify-export-surface]\n          [--certificate-artifact CERTIFICATE_ARTIFACT]\n          [target]\n\nLadon clean-core Lean analyzer\n\npositional arguments:\n  target                Optional analysis root alias\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --repo-root REPO_ROOT\n                        Repository root to analyze\n  --root ANALYSIS_ROOTS\n                        Lean root file or module; repeat for multi-root scope.\n  --scope {changed-set,closure,inventory,multi-root,namespace,owner}\n                        Primary/context population contract; owner is the\n                        ordinary default.\n  --changed-path CHANGED_PATH\n  --changed-manifest CHANGED_MANIFEST\n  --max-modules MAX_MODULES\n  --max-context-modules MAX_CONTEXT_MODULES\n  --cache-dir CACHE_DIR\n                        Source-index cache directory; defaults to the platform\n                        user cache.\n  --no-cache            Bypass source-index reads and writes for this\n                        analysis.\n  --build               Run the target repository's lake build before\n                        dependent analysis.\n  --build-timeout BUILD_TIMEOUT\n                        Finite Lake build deadline in seconds.\n  --extraction-backend {text,lean}\n                        Select text-only discovery or Lean-backed extraction.\n                        The Lean backend loads target environments and is\n                        unsafe for untrusted repositories.\n  --lean-extraction-scope {root,inventory}\n  --lean-cache-dir LEAN_CACHE_DIR\n                        Optional cache directory for Lean helper JSON payloads\n  --lean-batch-size LEAN_BATCH_SIZE\n                        Modules per bounded Lean inventory helper invocation\n                        (minimum 2).\n  --lean-timeout LEAN_TIMEOUT\n                        Finite deadline in seconds for each Lean helper batch.\n  --lean-strict         Reject partial Lean batches while preserving their\n                        rows and diagnostics.\n  --progress {auto,plain,json,off}\n                        Emit long-run progress on stderr; auto is interactive-\n                        only.\n  --overall-timeout OVERALL_TIMEOUT\n                        Optional finite deadline for the complete analysis in\n                        seconds.\n  --max-rss-mib MAX_RSS_MIB\n                        Optional supported process-tree resident-memory limit\n                        in MiB.\n  --max-report-bytes MAX_REPORT_BYTES\n                        Optional maximum bytes for each selected report\n                        representation.\n  --format {text,json}\n  --output OUTPUT       Report path, or - for standard output.\n  --emit FORMAT=PATH    Add an output destination; repeat for multiple report\n                        formats.\n  --report-version {v3,v2,v1}\n                        JSON report major. Canonical output defaults to v3;\n                        deprecated --json/--text output retains v2 unless\n                        selected explicitly.\n  --projection {summary,review,full}\n                        Report-v3 projection; review is the ordinary default.\n  --output-json LEGACY_JSON, --json LEGACY_JSON\n  --output-text LEGACY_TEXT, --text LEGACY_TEXT\n  --fail-on FAIL_ON     Repeatable kind:<kind>, severity:<minimum>, or\n                        phase:<name>:<skipped|partial> selector.\n  --generated-at-utc GENERATED_AT_UTC\n  --doc-file DOC_FILE\n  --packet-dir PACKET_DIR\n  --architecture-policy ARCHITECTURE_POLICY\n                        Optional JSON policy defining project-specific module\n                        groups and forbidden imports.\n  --source-pattern-policy SOURCE_PATTERN_POLICY\n                        Optional JSON policy defining project-specific source\n                        text patterns to report.\n  --generated-family-policy GENERATED_FAMILY_POLICY\n                        Optional versioned JSON policy defining project-\n                        generated source families and quoted provenance.\n  --generated-family-candidate-profile GENERATED_FAMILY_CANDIDATE_PROFILE\n                        Optional strict versioned profile for advisory\n                        generated-family candidate detection.\n  --module-system-witness MODULE_SYSTEM_WITNESS\n                        Optional JSON witness quoting Lean module-system\n                        boundary evidence.\n  --import-diet-witness IMPORT_DIET_WITNESS\n                        Optional JSON witness quoting Lean/Lake import\n                        minimization evidence.\n  --proof-xray PROOF_XRAY\n                        Optional JSON witness quoting elaborated proof-shape\n                        evidence.\n  --packet-profile {generic,review_packet,witness_bundle,release_bundle}\n                        Evidence profile used for --packet-dir summaries.\n  --verify-export-surface\n  --certificate-artifact CERTIFICATE_ARTIFACT\n\ncommands:\n  doctor    Emit read-only installation and repository readiness diagnostics.\n  result    Validate an experimental result manifest without loading Lean evidence.\n  theorem   Plan, materialize, and independently replay theorem capsules.\n  proof-search  Build and query local Lean proof-navigation evidence.\n  proofir       Validate, canonicalize, or inspect ProofIR artifacts.\n  runset    Execute a versioned set of ordinary analyses.\n  preview   Resolve roots, scope, policies, and costs without target execution.\n  inspect   Inspect canonical rows from one existing report or source index.\n  findings  List, filter, or inspect findings from one existing report.\n  atlas     Build an atlas from reports or a runset bundle.\n  query     Run a canned query against an atlas SQLite database.\n  diff      Compare two explicit atlas files structurally.\n  cards     Render reviewer cards from an atlas.\n  workflow  Build a combined atlas review workflow.\n\nRun 'ladon COMMAND --help' for command-specific options.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"verdict\": \"faithful\",\n  \"statementAssessment\": \"The exposition and supplied formal description assert the same identity for natural n. No statement discrepancy is apparent from the supplied text.\",\n  \"methodAssessment\": \"The exposition describes symmetric pairing; the formal description says the identity is proved by induction. These are different methods. The supplied formal text does not corroborate the exposition’s method, but that does not undermine the identity.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"For natural n, the sum of the integers from 1 to n is n(n+1)/2; the proof pairs terms symmetrically and handles a middle term when needed.\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"The supplied formal description says it proves the same identity by induction on n, adding n+1 and simplifying at the successor step.\",\n      \"classification\": \"valid different method\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The statement matches at the level described. Symmetric pairing and induction are distinct proof methods, and the formal description supports the identity by induction rather than documenting the pairing argument.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The input explicitly describes both methods. For the pairing method, terms k and n+1-k sum to n+1; when n is odd, the unpaired middle term is (n+1)/2. The report has no original Lean module or exact formal proposition to inspect.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"The formal counterpart is only a prose summary, so exact binder types, summation conventions, and proof details cannot be independently checked.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"examinedAssertions\": [\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“For natural n, the sum of the integers from 1 to n is n(n+1)/2.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"Faithfully matched by the supplied formal description, which says it proves the same identity.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Both descriptions state the sum formula for natural n; no conflicting domain or conclusion is stated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“The supplied proof pairs terms symmetrically, each pair summing to n+1, treating a middle term separately when needed.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"The pairing is a valid described method, but it is not the method given in the formal description.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Symmetric terms k and n+1-k sum to n+1; an odd number of terms leaves the middle term (n+1)/2. The formal description instead specifies induction.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"omissions\": \"The excerpt contains only the identity and its proof-method description. The formal input is a rendered prose summary, not an original Lean module, so exact formal syntax, dependencies, and implementation details are unavailable.\",\n  \"toolsUsed\": [\n    \"Read /procedure.md and /input/INPUT.md.\",\n    \"Read /tools/ladon --help; did not run an analysis because no Lean source or repository was supplied.\"\n  ],\n  \"checkingStatus\": \"No Lean checks were run or claimed. Assessment is based on the supplied text and elementary mathematical reasoning.\"\n}"}}
